50,3,1,talk,Rin,,Free Address sounds like a nightmare with the setup time. I'm against Option A.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C is the most budget-friendly since it minimizes the facilities charges for re-running power.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option B is fairer than A because it rotates the bad seats, but C is more stable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option A is out. I can't spend days adjusting a chair every time I move. I prefer C.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"Option C keeps the project strands together, which is great for the new joiners.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Rin,,"If we do Option B, do we still have to do the ""plugging in"" thing every time we shift?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Likely, and it would trigger those facilities costs again every time the block rotates.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, yes, but it prevents one person from being stuck by the noisy printer forever.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Shion,,I'd rather just have one good spot I can perfect than rotate through several mediocre ones.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I think Option C is the best for team communication.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Rin,,"Okay, if Option C means I don't have to move my stuff every morning, I'm in.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Toshio,,It is the most logical choice for the budget and the infrastructure.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"I still worry about the window seats, but we can assign them fairly in Option C.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Shion,,It's the only way to ensure the sound and physio issues are managed.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for C to keep our collaboration high.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Rin,,I'm sold on C!,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Toshio,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I'll go with C as well, provided we discuss the window assignments.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,4,talk,Shion,,C is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,4,talk,Yumi,,Definitely C!,"{""words"":2,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
